meta {
  name: Stripe Webhook (Stripe only)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/stripe
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Stripe-Signature: t=0,v1=placeholder
}

body:json {
  {
    "id": "evt_example",
    "type": "invoice.paid"
  }
}

docs {
  Not runnable from Bruno with a real result: the signature is verified against the exact
  raw bytes Stripe sent, computed with STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET. Any payload built here will
  fail verification and get a 400 — which is itself the check PricingSecurityTest asserts
  (webhookEsPublicoPeroExigeFirma).

  To exercise this endpoint for real, use the Stripe CLI against a locally running server:
    stripe listen --forward-to localhost:8080/api/v1/webhooks/stripe
    stripe trigger invoice.paid

  This request exists in the collection purely to document the contract: unauthenticated,
  POST, raw-string body, Stripe-Signature header required.
}
